Scenario A: Basic Mixed Workload

 Input Data:

o P1: Arrival=0, Burst=6, Priority=2
o P2: Arrival=2, Burst=2, Priority=1
o P3: Arrival=4, Burst=3, Priority=3

 Description
"This scenario confirms the fundamental logic of the three algorithms.
In SJF Non-Preemptive, P1 finishes entirely before P2 starts,
whereas in SJF Preemptive, P2 interrupts P1 at time 2 because it is shorter.
Meanwhile, Priority scheduling focuses on the priority values regardless of the burst duration." 
